  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Reconstruction program Ukraine, BE-Relieve</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR"></narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. &#x201c;The construction and energy sectors are strengthened in their recovery efforts and progressively transition towards a decarbonized and circular economy, contributing to Ukraine&apos;s long-term resilience and sustainability&#x201d;
2. &#x201c;The continuation of inclusive basic services is supported in the fields of health 
and social protection&#x201d;
3. &#x201c;The continuation of inclusive education and vocational training is ensured, and the provision and effective employment of an adequately skilled workforce for the recovery process is enhanced.&#x201d;
4. Key issues such as environmental sustainability, gender equality, local governance and resilience related to the security context will be mainstreamed throughout the program. 
5. Ukraine&#x2019;s reform agenda is supported, with a focus on the country&#x2019;s pathway 
to accession into the European Union, while cooperation between Ukrainian and Belgian public actors is strengthened, fostering ties as future EU partners.
 to be determined</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Be-Relieve programme is designed to advance Ukraine&apos;s green reconstruction and recovery by fostering resilience, sustainability, and inclusivity across key sectors, while aligning with the nation&apos;s path towards European Union membership. The intervention areas will be the Kyiv region, Kyiv capital city and the Chernihiv region. Enabel will work in:
Domain 1: Energy and Circular Construction
Domain 2: Health and Social protection 
Domain 3: Education, Skills and Decent Employment
Cross-Cutting Themes and EU Accession &amp; Acquis Communautaire including Build Back Better The general objective of the BE-RELIEVE program is to contribute to the sustainable reconstruction and recovery of Ukraine. The specific objective is to &quot;accelerate green reconstruction and recovery, and enable the return, protection, and development of the targeted populations.&quot;
The program proposes a flexible approach, given the volatile context in which it will operate. BE-RELIEVE will work in the following major areas: energy efficiency, reconstruction, health, social protection, education, and employment. This is organized into three pillars: (1) construction and rehabilitation; (2) basic health and social protection services; and (3) general and vocational education and skilled labor. The primary focus will be on the Chernihiv region, and by extension, Kyiv, but work will also be carried out at the national level, depending on Ukraine&apos;s needs. Depending on the situation, the program&apos;s geographical focus may be further expanded.</narrative>
  </description>
